[size=150][b]Enphase Envoy Plugin for Indigo Domotics[/b][/size]

Monitor your Enphase solar system — production, consumption, battery, and individual panel output — directly from [url=https://www.indigodomo.com/]Indigo Domotics[/url] via your local Envoy gateway. No cloud dependency; data updates every 60 seconds.

[url=https://github.com/Ghawken/IndigoEnphaseEnvoy/releases/latest]Latest Release[/url] | [url=http://www.indigodomo.com/pluginstore/105/]Indigo Plugin Store[/url] | [url=https://github.com/Ghawken/IndigoEnphaseEnvoy/wiki]Full Wiki Documentation[/url]

[size=120][b]Features[/b][/size]

[list]
[*][b]Real-time solar monitoring[/b] — production, consumption, net flow, and grid status updated every 60 seconds direct from the local Envoy
[*][b]Per-panel microinverter devices[/b] — one Indigo device per panel, showing watts, temperature, DC/AC voltage, energy totals, and last-heard time
[*][b]Battery & grid support[/b] — full Encharge battery state, charge/discharge rate, state of charge, storage mode, and grid import/export
[*][b]Cost tracking[/b] — optional Cost device calculates daily, 7-day, and lifetime energy costs against your configured tariff rates
[*][b]Power production control[/b] — enable or disable all inverter output via an Indigo action (installer token required)
[*][b]DPEL — Dynamic Power Export Limiting[/b] — cap grid export or total production at a configurable watt limit and slew rate
[*][b]Battery storage mode control[/b] — switch between Self-Consumption, Savings (TOU), and Full Backup; enable/disable grid charging; set reserve SOC
[*][b]Firmware ≥7 JWT authentication[/b] — auto-generates and refreshes installer or owner tokens; supports manual token entry
[*][b]Multi-Envoy[/b] — run multiple Envoy devices simultaneously for homes with more than one gateway
[*][b]No external dependencies[/b] — all required packages are bundled inside the plugin; no manual pip installs needed
[/list]

