[size=120][b]Quick Start[/b][/size]

[list=1]
[*][b]Download[/b] the latest [url=https://github.com/Ghawken/IndigoEnphaseEnvoy/releases/latest].indigoPlugin from GitHub Releases[/url] or from the [url=http://www.indigodomo.com/pluginstore/105/]Indigo Plugin Store[/url].
[*][b]Double-click[/b] the downloaded file — Indigo will prompt to install and enable it.
[*][b]Create a device[/b] — go to [i]Devices → New Device…[/i], select model [b]Enphase Envoy-S[/b], and enter your Envoy's local IP address.
[*][b]Add a token[/b] (firmware ≥7 only) — use [b]Generate Token[/b] with your Enphase Enlighten credentials, or paste a manual token from [url=https://entrez.enphaseenergy.com/]entrez.enphaseenergy.com[/url].
[*][b]Save[/b] — the plugin polls immediately; within 30 seconds [i]deviceIsOnline[/i] will be True and live data will appear.
[/list]

Full step-by-step instructions: [url=https://github.com/Ghawken/IndigoEnphaseEnvoy/wiki/Installation-and-Setup]Installation & Setup wiki page[/url]

