[size=120][b]Supported Device Types[/b][/size]

[list]
[*][b]Enphase Envoy-S[/b] — Main gateway: production, consumption, storage, per-phase metering
[*][b]Enphase Legacy[/b] — Older Envoy-C hardware without metering support
[*][b]Enphase Panel[/b] — One device per microinverter: watts, temperature, DC/AC voltage, energy totals
[*][b]Enphase Battery & Grid[/b] — Encharge battery state, grid flow, storage mode settings
[*][b]Enphase Cost[/b] — Calculates energy costs against your tariff rates
[/list]

[size=120][b]What's New — v1.8.0[/b][/size]

[list]
[*][b]Menu item: Log Last Time Envoy Heard from Panels[/b] — highlights panels that have gone silent and shows reporting delay
[*]New states: [i]panelLastUpdated[/i], [i]panelLastUpdatedUTC[/i], [i]panelDataSource[/i]
[*]New state: [i]grid_text[/i] — human-readable summary e.g. [i]"Grid in use & Importing 450 Watts"[/i]
[*]New states: [i]grid_in_use[/i] (Boolean) and [i]grid_usage[/i] (signed watts)
[*][i]powerStatus[/i] neutral band — flows under 100 W classified as [i]neutral[/i] rather than importing/exporting
[*]Bug fix: voltage states were not divided by phase count on multi-phase systems
[/list]

Full changelog: [url=https://github.com/Ghawken/IndigoEnphaseEnvoy/releases]GitHub Releases[/url]

[size=120][b]Requirements[/b][/size]

[list]
[*][b]Indigo Domotics[/b] 2025.1+
[*][b]Python[/b] 3.10+ (bundled with modern Indigo)
[*][b]Network[/b] — Indigo Mac and Envoy must be on the same LAN
[*][b]Enphase account[/b] — required only for firmware ≥7 token generation
[/list]

[size=120][b]Actions at a Glance[/b][/size]

[list]
[*]Refresh all devices / Refresh single device — [i]any token[/i]
[*]Enable / Disable power production — [b]installer token required[/b]
[*]Enable / Disable DPEL (export limiting) — [b]installer token required[/b]
[*]Set storage mode (self-consumption / savings / backup) — installer token recommended
[*]Enable / Disable charge from grid — installer token recommended
[*]Set battery reserve SOC — installer token recommended
[/list]

Full parameter details and workflow examples: [url=https://github.com/Ghawken/IndigoEnphaseEnvoy/wiki/Actions-Reference]Actions Reference[/url]

